---------------------
!अथ तिलकः 


```
देवताभ्य इति । सुप्तोत्थितवदुप्तिष्ठन्तु वानरा इत्येवंरूपं वरं रावणवधजनितहर्षवशात्स्वदिदृक्षया समागताभ्यो देवताभ्यः प्राप्य सुहृद्भिः सुप्रीवविभीषणादिभिः संवृतः पुष्पकेणायोध्यामुदि्दश्य प्रस्थितो जगाम ॥
```


Step-by-Step Translation:


<<<
देवताभ्य इति । (From the deities, thus/this was the context.)

"सुप्तोत्थितवदुप्तिष्ठन्तु वानराः" इत्येवंरूपं वरम्... (The boon whose form was, "Let the monkeys rise up as if awakened from sleep"—...)

...रावणवधजनितहर्षवशात्... (...out of the joy born from the slaying of Rāvaṇa...)

...स्वदिदृक्षया समागताभ्यो देवताभ्यः प्राप्य... (...having obtained (this boon) from the deities who had assembled due to their desire to see him (Rāma)...)

...सुहृद्भिः सुप्रीवविभीषणादिभिः संवृतः... (...surrounded by his friends, such as Sugrīva, Vibhīṣaṇa, and others...)

...पुष्पकेणायोध्यामुदि्दश्य प्रस्थितो जगाम। (...set out for Ayodhyā by the Puṣpaka Vimāna and departed/went.)
<<<


Meaningful Translation:

>Rāma, having received a boon from the assembled deities—who had come out of joy born from the slaying of Rāvaṇa and their desire to see him—stating, "Let the monkeys rise up as if awakened from sleep," then, surrounded by his friends like Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa, set out for Ayodhyā by the Puṣpaka Vimāna and departed.

📝 व्याकरण-विश्लेषणम् (Grammatical Analysis)


<<<
देवताभ्यः (Dēvatābhyaḥ): पञ्चमी-बहुवचनम् (Ablative Plural), "from the deities."

सुप्तोत्थितवत् (Suptōtthitavat): अव्ययम् (Indeclinable), "like one awakened from sleep."

समागताभ्यः (Samāgatābhyaḥ): चतुर्थी/पञ्चमी-बहुवचनम् (Dative/Ablative Plural), देवताभ्यः इत्यस्य विशेषणम्। (Who had assembled).

प्राप्य (Prāpya): ल्यप्-अव्ययम् (Lyap Indeclinable), "having obtained/received."

संवृतः (Saṁvr̥taḥ): क्त-प्रत्ययान्तः (Kta Participle), "surrounded (by)."

पुष्पकेण (Puṣpakēṇa): तृतीया-एकवचनम् (Instrumental Singular), "by means of the Puṣpaka (Vimāna)."

उदि्दश्य (Udiśya): ल्यप्-अव्ययम् (Lyap Indeclinable), "having aimed at/for the purpose of" (Ayodhyā).

जगाम (Jagāma): √गम् धातोः लिट्-लकारः (Perfect Tense of √gam), "went/departed."
<<<
